/**
 * @page usage_page Using Softloq UTF-8
 *
 * @section usage_consuming Consuming the Library
 * Add this repository as a subdirectory of your own CMake project and link against the
 * `Softloq::UTF-8` target:
 *
 * @code{.cmake}
 * add_subdirectory(path/to/softloq-utf-8)
 * target_link_libraries(consumer PRIVATE Softloq::UTF-8)
 * @endcode
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * #include "softloq/utf-8/utf-8.hpp"
 * @endcode
 *
 * If you consume the default shared build (i.e. `SOFTLOQ_UTF_8_BUILD_STATIC` is `OFF`), define
 * `SOFTLOQ_UTF_8_IMPORTS` when compiling your own sources against the library's headers:
 *
 * @code{.cmake}
 * target_compile_definitions(consumer PRIVATE SOFTLOQ_UTF_8_IMPORTS)
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section usage_workflow Typical Workflow
 * Decode raw UTF-8 bytes into a validated softloq::utf_8::Char, or encode a validated Char back into
 * bytes, through the softloq::utf_8::decode() and softloq::utf_8::encode() facade functions. Every
 * fallible step returns `std::expected<Value, softloq::utf_8::Error>`, so malformed input is handled
 * explicitly rather than thrown as an exception.
 *
 * @section usage_examples Examples & Tests
 * See the [examples/](https://github.com/Softloq/UTF-8/tree/main/examples) directory for runnable
 * programs demonstrating the public API, and the
 * [tests/](https://github.com/Softloq/UTF-8/tree/main/tests) directory for the GoogleTest suite
 * covering `Octet`, `OctetSequence`, `Char`, and the `decode()`/`encode()` facade.
 */
